<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ziusudra</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Utnapishtim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ziusudra is the hero of the Sumerian flood story, a king of Shuruppak warned by the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enki">Enki</a> to build a great boat and save life from the deluge. Afterwards the gods granted him eternal life and settled him in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilmun">Dilmun</a>, where the sun rises. In the Akkadian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epic-of-gilgamesh">Epic of Gilgamesh</a> the same figure appears as Utnapishtim, whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilgamesh">Gilgamesh</a> visits in search of immortality.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ziusudra.jpg" alt="Ziusudra" width="320" height="585" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gts-tg · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sumerian_King_List,_1800_BC,_Larsa,_Iraq_(detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
